# walking_dead_remastered_le 0.92 - Spike 3 (64-bit ARM): drafted by s3port.py (PAD-1287) from the Spike 3 port star_wars_elg-1.10.port (star_wars_elg 1.10).
# Functions paired across the two titles: 9463 of 18297 reference functions (7964 anchored by vtable slots and strings, 377 through calls that line up, the rest grown through calls); half of them line up 100% or better.
# Written: what the reference port carries that is the FRAMEWORK's (each site's function at least 75% alike its
# reference's, each global and offset read at the lined-up instruction, the engines' layouts re-read off this program's
# own code); the switch lines from this program's own device table. The reference game's own content (shows, lamps,
# callouts, scenes, held coils, its modes) is not this title's: written as comments, for its own port.
# Emulator-proven 2026-11-15 (PAD-1287) on the Spike 3 rig (s3run.sh, slot 37, hidden, muted; PAD_S3_MODE_SO = a 64-bit
# build of template_mode.c): the runtime took this port (29 sites, 32 shots), held back the Insider achievement query
# (type 28), armed the 6 events with the dispatch hooked and both switch_hit sites; in play TARGET RUSH started on the
# third Tower target hit (switch 54), scored 6 shots through the game's score_add (+21,000,000: the score table read
# 90,560 at its start, 22,214,100 at the next) and ended on the end of the ball (bus event 0x34); a second run ended
# on its clock, and the game played on to the 480 s cap (ball 2, 43,350,600). Program sha1
# bcf428e162bfec6add82aac519f5f93968d0e283 (games/game).
# Sounds emulator-proven 2026-11-15 (PAD-1287, slot 37, muted): requests 150, 160 and 170 played on the game's own channels
# (buses b02 / b04 in the runtime's channel read), sound_active answered 1 while each played, sound_stop and a fade over
# 800 ms ended them (active 0 within a second), and the callout site played 160.
# Multiball emulator-proven 2026-11-15 (PAD-1287): a mode.cfg `multiball 3 10` started on three Tower target hits, the
# game served to 3 balls in play (trough 3/6), the mode scored 3 shots (+6,000,000), counted 3 -> 2 -> 1 balls and gave
# the game its multiball back. Lamps (no lamp lines yet), the game's shows, screens and clips are this title's own work.
# PAD-1292 2026-11-15 (Spike 3 rig slot 93, hidden, muted): multiball again (3 served, +6,000,000, its clock, handed back
# at one ball) and the ball save (15 s save taken, the drain inside it served back, 3 shots +6,000,000, the drain after
# it ended the ball; the control ended on its first drain). The Write: write_card put WALKER RUSH (Tower target x3,
# Left loop / Right loop / Right spinner, 25 s) on a copy of the card, read back through its own encryption
# (/games/game -> pad/padmode/padmode.sh, game.target walking_dead_remastered_le/game); that card booted through its
# own hook, the runtime read this port off it, the mode started on the third Tower target hit, scored 9 shots
# (90,560 -> 45,341,900) and ended on its clock. Not proven: a mode waiting out the game's own multiball (no switch
# route tried started one of Blood Bath / Prison / Well). This port carries no mode books of Star Wars ELG's (PAD-1292:
# s3port lined its flags 66 / 68 up by number, which are other flags here).

game           walking_dead_remastered_le
version        0.92

